{"source_key":"sha256-767aea33d36d18c60bf3118db432de90","record_index":36,"record_hash":"sha256:1f06c0753a7d60918466e863086a27e95e6682e708b4f14f1a82088c0a679651","timestamp":"2026-07-23T14:32:31.186Z","kind":"tool_result","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:custom_tool_call_output","role":null,"text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.0 seconds\nOutput:\n\n{\"issue\":{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"GB-1753\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Caleb's Worktree Experiment\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Spec given to LLM\\\\n\\\\nI would like to work on adding experimental worktree support into GitButler.\\\\n\\\\n## Feature flag\\\\n\\\\nIn [settings.rs](<http://settings.rs>), we will have an `worktreeManipulation` feature flag.\\\\n\\\\nThe user will be able to set it by changing the settings.json file manually initially.\\\\n\\\\n## Metadata:\\\\n\\\\nWe want to avoid displaying way too many worktrees. As such, we're going to store some data in our database to help curb this.\\\\n\\\\nWe will have a table that keys off of a worktree (path? - that is the primary identifier git/gix has for them?). Worktrees will either be archived or not.\\\\n\\\\nThe first time we read the worktrees for a project, we will mark all existing worktrees as archived since they are probably old.\\\\n\\\\n## Operations on worktrees:\\\\n\\\\n* archive\\\\n* unarchive\\\\n\\\\n## Tie into but graph\\\\n\\\\nWe want commits in worktrees to be traversed in the but-graph.\\\\n\\\\nIf `worktreeManipulation` is set, we will include all non-archived worktrees as extra traversal heads when creating the but graph.\\\\n\\\\n## Tie into the editor (but-rebase)\\\\n\\\\nWe keep track of the HEADs that we want to check out.\\\\n\\\\nWe will add a new variant to the `Checkout` enum `Worktree` which will describe a worktree checkout.\\\\n\\\\nWhen we materialize, we will use `safe_checkout` to also checkout the worktrees.\\\\n\\\\nBy default, we won't list or checkout worktrees in the checkouts array and only set them when the feature flag is set.\\\\n\\\\n## but-workspace API for listing worktrees\\\\n\\\\nWe will have an API that makes use of the but-graph in order to list the worktrees.\\\\n\\\\nIt will:\\\\n\\\\n* obtain a list of all the worktrees\\\\n* determine which are archived and which are not\\\\n* for those that are not archived, it will perform a traversal `worktree_head ^target_commit_id` or simply `worktree_head` as a first parent traversal over the\n[TRUNCATED]\n82d49c4ea0\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"100%\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-17T13:43:35.067Z\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-17T13:43:35.026Z\\\",\\\"parentId\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"resolvedAt\\\":null,\\\"quotedText\\\":null,\\\"author\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Caleb Owens\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"It would be nice to have the option of applying a worktree to your workspace, and have your agent continue to do work in that worktree and have the changes continuously appear in your workspace. You have the best of both: agent isolation, but let the user keep their megamerge.\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-16T15:18:03.828Z\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-17T13:43:35.095Z\\\",\\\"parentId\\\":null,\\\"resolvedAt\\\":null,\\\"quotedText\\\":null,\\\"author\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Olly\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"Consider how worktees can be also part of the worktees \\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-16T14:44:28.620Z\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-16T14:44:28.592Z\\\",\\\"parentId\\\":null,\\\"resolvedAt\\\":null,\\\"quotedText\\\":null,\\\"author\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Caleb Owens\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"Should tell us about conflicts between worktrees\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-16T14:44:05.487Z\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-16T14:44:05.468Z\\\",\\\"parentId\\\":null,\\\"resolvedAt\\\":null,\\\"quotedText\\\":null,\\\"author\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Caleb Owens\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"Prototype build here: [gitbutlerapp/gitbutler#14789](https://linear.[REDACTED:entropy])\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-16T11:00:04.573Z\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-07-16T11:00:04.556Z\\\",\\\"parentId\\\":null,\\\"resolvedAt\\\":null,\\\"quotedText\\\":null,\\\"author\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"[REDACTED:entropy]\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Caleb Owens\\\"}}],\\\"hasNextPage\\\":false}\"}],\"isError\":false}}","tool_name":"exec","tool_kind":"other","tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-07-23T14:32:31.186Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","call_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]"}}}}